/** @page dev-overview Overview

With VidRe, acquisition and control are separated as backend and frontend, 
respectively. They backend is implemented as a service 
[daemon](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daemon_(computing)) 
(src/apps/daemon) that is responsible for acquisition without requiring a 
graphical display (suitable for embedded use). 
The frontend provides two options, either a command-line interface 
(src/apps/cli)
or a graphical user-interface 
(src/apps/gui). Additional tools, for example to convert a video stream to MP4, are
provided (src/apps/tools).

Core functionality is provided in C++ (at least [C++20](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/20),
see @ref api). At the moment of writing, the main system targets are Linux® and 
Windows®. For graphical user-interface applications [Qt6](https://www.qt.io/product/framework) 
is used. 

The objective is to provide a videography software suite, that allows to record 
scientifically relevant data from different types of video sources including 
supplemental information and data streams (such as timing, audio, etc.). 
Ultimately we aim at a modular framework that allows to supplement real-time 
features, such as object recognition combined with feedback.

*/
